    tables = '\n'.join((f"| {x['case'].replace('ToothFairy2', '')}/cc{x['component']} | {x['reference_gap_mm']:.3f} | {x['minimum_connected_added_voxels']} | {x['adverse_gap_mm']:.3f} | {100 * x['Dice_adverse']:.4f}% | {x['HD95_adverse_mm']:.1f} |" for x in pairs))
    budget = '\n'.join((f"| {x['case'].replace('ToothFairy2', '')} | {x['field']['dangerous_cells']} | {x['field']['measurement_cells']} | {100 * x['field']['measurement_cell_fraction']:.3f}% |" for x in fields))
    results = {'lane': 'X5-decision-seg-error', 'review_state': 'PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW', 'capability': 'Model-independent local directed edge-error tolerance, whole-mask decision flips, and exact minimum connected addition counterexample in fixed annotated geometry', 'outcome': 'THREE_EXECUTED_CONSTRUCTIONS; USEFUL_GEOMETRIC_CAPABILITY; STRONG_CONTROLS_TIE; PHYSICAL_CALIBRATION_FAIL_OR_UNKNOWN; NO_EMPIRICAL_10X_CLAIM', 'external_referent': {'kind': 'independent_measurement', 'locator': 'https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-20605-w', 'compared_quantity': 'Published highest-pair SMCD median 0.77 mm is compared to the proposed local maximum directed canal-wall error bound. The observables do not match; transport as a safety bound is rejected.', 'refutes_us': True}, 'external_referents': [r2['external_referent'], r3['own_fixture_referent'], {'kind': 'independent_measurement', 'locator': 'https://doi.org/10.1007/s00784-022-04708-2', 'compared_quantity': 'Combined anatomy interobserver refinement HD95 0.045 mm versus local maximum tooth/pulp error; invalid interchange', 'refutes_us': True}, {'kind': 'independent_measurement', 'locator': 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.joen.2021.09.001', 'compared_quantity': 'Pulp ASD 0.08 mm and HD 1.99 mm in microCT-guided study; mean error cannot certify the local 0.057591 mm margin of a separate STS-derived case', 'refutes_us': True}], 'rounds': [r1, r2, r3], 'scan_count_archived': len({r['case'] for r in records}), 'archive_snapshot_scope': '2342 sites in338 represented scans from369 archive files; not all480 TF2 scans. Different archived snapshot from F lane2305/337; all sourcefiles retained and hashes bound.', 'guard_status_counts_RB': dict(status), 'missing_source_guards_RB': sum((len(r.get('missing_regions', [])) for r in rb)), 'tightest_preparation_guard': tight, 'nonempty_R2_measurement_sets': sum((x['field']['dangerous_cells'] > 0 for x in fields)), 'data_artifacts': data + data3 + [ex], 'numerical_artifact_hashes': {n: sha(P / n) for n in ['RAW_R1_SITE_GUARDS.jsonl', 'DECISION_MARGINS.csv', 'PREPARATION_MARGINS.csv', 'R1_CONTROLS.json', 'RAW_R2_FIELDS.json', 'R2_GLOBAL_METRIC_COUNTEREXAMPLES.json', 'R2_N_WITNESS_PORT.json', 'R3_CONNECTED_COUNTEREXAMPLES.json', 'VERIFICATION.json']}, 'prereg_and_prediction_hashes': {n: sha(P / n) for n in ['PREREG_R1.json', 'PREREG_R2.json', 'PREREG_R3.json', 'FROZEN_PREDICTIONS.json', 'FROZEN_PREDICTIONS_R3.json']}, 'cost': {'last_complete_rounds_wall_seconds_sum': sum((r['cost']['wall_seconds'] for r in [r1, r2, r3])), 'last_complete_rounds_cpu_seconds_sum': sum((r['cost']['cpu_seconds'] for r in [r1, r2, r3])), 'peak_rss_kib': max((r['cost']['peak_rss_kib'] for r in [r1, r2, r3])), 'threads_max': 1, 'GPU': False, 'data_intermediates_bytes': sum((x['bytes'] for x in data + data3 + [ex])), 'prior_failed_and_control_replay_invocations': 'Preserved in versions and run_r2_control_replay.log; not hidden in speed ratio; no exact total including failed prefix', 'prior_annotation_segmentation_EDT_search_and_manual_literature_review_seconds': None, 'lab_measurement_or_independent_review_seconds': None}, 'limitations': ['Fixed submitted masks are fully measured; true hazard coverage is UNKNOWN', 'Error injections demonstrate possibility, not model error frequency', 'Minimum connected addition applies only to six-neighbour unconstrained false-positive paths', 'Thresholds and error distributions are closures/scenarios', 'R1 max-slack choice has no guarantee for original stochastic risk, anchorage, mechanics or full continuous catalogue search', 'Four of six R2 measurement sets are empty; no observed laboratory acquisition gain', 'All constructions share adaptive inherited TF2 cohort; not a blind confirmatory validation'], 'next_construction': 'Freeze one actual segmentation model output, obtain independently measured/reviewed local canal-wall or pulp surface over the dangerous patch plus complete hazard coverage, and run assess_model.py without fitting to its held-out result.'}
    put('results.json', results)
    readme = f"# Segmenteringsfel i beslutsenheter\n\nA segmentation shall be able to be assessed against the fixed geometry decision for which it is used. The tool gives direction and edge error in mm that reaches a declared limit, shows which local channel surfaces can affect the decision and constructs the smallest continuous mask expansion that alters it. Physical security is **UNKNOWN**.\n\n```bash\n./run_all.sh\n```\n\nDriving takes about two minutes here, with a thread and about 1,1 GB topp-RAM. Requires local dataset/soesophagus SOURCE_SMALL_MANIFEST and SOURCE_DESIGN_MANIFEST, Python med NumPy/SciPy and the system's Matplotlib. No datasets are retrieved. Frozen contracts and inputhas are checked before rerun.\n\n| Resultat | Utfall |\n|---|---|\n| Arkiverad implantatgeometri | {r1['counts']['source_sites']} platser, {results['scan_count_archived']} representerade skanningar, {r1['counts']['source_candidates']:,} kandidater |\n| Beslutsregioner | {r1['selected_guard_rows']} implant rows and {r1['prep_guard_rows']} preparationsrader |\n| Invers limit to scalar control | maximum difference {r1['scalar_control_max_error_mm']:.2g} mm; TIE |\n| Precise local channel distance | sex frysta fall; direkt allparskontroll ≤1,5·10⁻¹⁴ mm |\n| Coherent errors that reverse 2 mm-regeln | {min(r3['minimum_added_voxels'])}–{max(r3['minimum_added_voxels'])} voxlar i sex av sex motprov |\n| Global dimensions in each counterexample | exakt samma Dice i fel/kontroll; HD95 = 0 for both |\n| Fysisk kantkalibrering | FAIL/UNKNOWN; published quantities cannot be local error limits |\n\n{chr(10)}![Resultat](DECISION_ERROR_FIGURE.png)\n\n| TF2-fall/komponent | Ursprungligt gap mm | Minsta nya voxlar | Gap efter fel mm | Dice fel/kontroll | HD95 mm |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n{tables}\n\nBase geometry comes from published [ToothFairy2-annotationer](https://ditto.ing.unimore.it/toothfairy2/), with independent replay against J's preserved full mask distance. The new bug masks are **injektioner**, not measured model error or an external anatomical reference observation. The smallest extensions match exactly to an independent binary-dilation control and survive selection of the channel's original component.\n\nMathematics is `m_i = d_i − t`. For a fixed design and a local arbitrary misdirection, the unfavorable boundary is the distance to the surface of the decision. A continuous addition must contain a path from the original channel to any voxel with cube spacing. `< t`; the shortest path gives the minimum number of new voxlar. Similarity `d=t` accepted; specified mm limits are infima to reverse an approved decision.\n\nA model can be assessed with:\n\n```bash\npython3 assess_model.py --input geometry_and_prediction.npz --threshold-mm 2 --reference-kind annotation --output decision_error.json\n```\n\nNPZ contains `body_mask`, `reference_hazard_mask`, `prediction_hazard_mask` as binary 3D-arrays on identical basis z/y/x-rutneat and `spacing_zyx_mm`; alternativt solida heltalskoordinater `body_voxel`, `reference_hazard_voxel`, `prediction_hazard_voxel`. For the depth of preparation, the fixed cut preparation surface shall be supplied as an object, the pulp as a hazard. `MODEL_EVALUATION_EXAMPLE.json` shows decisions, errors in mm, dangerous direction and reference status. No model training or afterfit is done.\n\nThe one that doesn't hold: Dice/HD95 does not guarantee border decisions; the published channel value [0,77 mm](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-20605-w) is a ban agent, not a local wall maximum. [0,045 mm HD95](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00784-022-04708-2) concerns common model refinements of several structures; [pulpa-ASD 0,08 mm](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.joen.2021.09.001) none of them certifies a single pulpahorn. STS-baserad LS2/M1 mesial margin is only {float(tight['signed_margin_mm']):.6f} mm and has no local external reference sightings.\n\nMeasurement patches use an explicit 0,77 mm scenario. Only two cases have non-empty patches, {100 * fields[3]['field']['measurement_cell_fraction']:.3f}% and {100 * fields[5]['field']['measurement_cell_fraction']:.3f}% Four empty sets mean that the annotated margin exceeds this scenario; they are no measured measurement savings. Anatomically missing surfaces, metalblooming, manufacturer-identified implant body and registration errors remain.\n\nData/licens: ToothFairy2 **CC BY-SA 4.0** according to local dataset.json, reuse koordinater/figurer follows attribute and ShareAlike. STS-3D-Tooth **CC BY 4.0** enligt [lokal README](../../data/corpus/geometry/STS-3D-Tooth/README.md) and [Wang et al.](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-024-04306-9). STS-pulpa i PROC_prep is a derived image segmentation, no published pulp mask. No Bits2Bites, mandibeldefekt, Teeth3DS or MMDental are used. Only data set keys, no personal data.\n\nAll thresholds are research conventions.–channel boundary 2 mm is different from the original stochastic drilling zone 1 Maximum geometry margin does not optimise anchoring or clinical risk. No clinical advice, scientific remission or empirical 10×-resultat ges. Status: PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. The next measurement is given in: MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_PORT.md.\n"
    (P / 'README_DEMO.md').write_text(readme)
    (P / 'RESULTS.md').write_text(f"# X5 — executable decision representation, physical calibration open\n\nThree frozen structures have been run. R1 makes edge errors to inverse limits on {r1['counts']['source_sites']} places and {r1['prep_guard_rows']} preparationsregioner. R2 retains all local channel areas and directions. R3 constructs the exact smallest connected error against the same bound. The strong controls with the same information give TIEThe ability lies in the response level and the new local measurement contract, not a new superior solver.\n\nSe README_DEMO.md for table, figure and run. R3:s six pairs have identical global dimensions but different decisions, with 2–11 connected added voxlar. These are synthetic counterexamples on published base geometry, not external mismeasurements. {r1['scalar_control_max_error_mm']:.2g} mm; direct all-pair control, frozen predictions and injected errors are found in the crude artefacts.\n\nExternal reference sightings are strictly typed. TF2 gives annotation, J preserved full mask metrology. DOI10.1038/s41598-022-20605-w, Nogueira-Reis DOI10.1007/s00784-022-04708-2 and flax DOI10.1016/j.joen.2021.09.001 gives published measurements of other, explicitly named quantities. medel/p95 to local max error. Physical local calibration for TF2/STS is UNKNOWNNo local clinical safety can be derived.\n\nR1 har {len(rb)} arkiverade RB-val. Kanalregion: fem nominellt under den nya kropp–the channel boundary; 27 ytterligare icke-negativa marginaler under0,22mm. Benregion: 194 marginaler under0,22mm. Granntand: 275 under0,22This is fixed geometryguards, not rerun of K37:s stokastiska borr-/guidebeslut. Saknade ±99 fields must remain UNKNOWN. The first wrong sentinel outcome is preserved in versions/.\n\nR2Only two non-empty outcomes can show local concentration under the assumed per-cell budget, and nothing shows actual lab measurement savings. N's supported contour points are reused through a one-sided upper-witness contract; all false full-surface approvals are rejected.\n\nCosts in results.json include preparation reading, detection and strong control calculations. No fit costs. Inherited annotation/search/EDT-work, literature reading, physical measurement and independent review are unmeasured and not excluded. {results['cost']['last_complete_rounds_wall_seconds_sum']:.2f}s; maxRSS {results['cost']['peak_rss_kib'] / 1024 ** 2:.3f}GiB, a thread, no one GPU. Bug prefix and extra control replay are preserved; no speed head start is claimed.\n\nVetenskaplig status PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. The next design is real model prediction against independent local channel/pulpa reference, before afterfit, with anatomical coverage sport. HANDOFF.md.\n")
    (P / 'MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_PORT.md').write_text("# Minimum independent local measuring port\n\nThe Capability that is still missing is to classify a real segmentation model's decision as robust against anatomical error. A 2mm convention is a comparative condition, no nerve damage threshold.\n\nFirst freeze model version, input/outputhash, fixed CAD/design/platform, regional identities, decision threshold, all critical patches from `decision_report`, coordinate transform and any expected margin in FROZEN_PREDICTIONS_NEXT.json. Separate the fit and final validation data; do not change criteria against the reference outcome.\n\nChannel lab reference: a scanner/protocol matched reference body with separate radial/apic metal metrology, actual implant body CAD/apex and a known channel surrogate surface with industrial CT or other independent metrology. For tooth/pulp : same tooth scan in CBCT and μCT, registered without using the critical pulp limit as a fit target. Save the entire hazard area and the localized maximum errors; mean/ HD95 is not enough. Independent expert contours on the same CBCT measure annotator variation, not automatic anatomical truth.\n\nPer patch you need reference area + targeted residual, fixed item error, registration, measurement resolution and a defensive simultaneous upper error budget. The parts that come from the same image/ source must not become independent repetitions. The requirement is `m_i > B_canal,i + B_object,i + B_registration,i + B_numeric,i` for each point. A single critical residual over the margin can reject prediction. An absent hazard/coverage port rejects all physical approval rating.\n\nUnder R2 : s assumed maximum displacement B for unquestioned surface cells is exactly dangerous set `d_i − t <= B` . Each such cell/patch must be anchored; if one is left unsettled, a permissible adversarial shift may reverse the decision. If another known cell has `d_i−t>B`, it cannot reverse under the same assumption. This is a conditional adequacy/minimumity result, no measured physical error limit. Missing anatomical parts and change of topology require full surface control.\n\nDeliver the same z/y/x-grid to `assess_model.py` for a frozen model precision and the independent reference. Report real fake approvals per design/region and scan, not just candidate change. In addition, check a error value such as +0,05 mm margin, error transform and omitted hazard patch — all must reject . Before a registered such measurement is physical status UNKNOWN .\n")
    (P / 'HANDOFF.md').write_text(f"# X5 handoff\n\nRun `./run_all.sh`. README_DEMO ger idé→tabell→figur→restriction. Three frozen and completed designs: R1 Inverse boundaries, R2 fulla lokala riktningar/mEat patches, R3 Exactly the smallest continuous vox expansion. {r1['counts']['source_sites']} platser/{results['scan_count_archived']} skanningar/{r1['counts']['source_candidates']} kandidater; {r1['selected_guard_rows']} Implant regions; and {r1['prep_guard_rows']} preparationsrader. Starka kontroller TIE. Sex/six coherent counterexample provides different decisions with identical Dice and HD95=0; minsta fel2–11voxlar.\n\nWhat fell: physical local calibration from published SMCD/HD95/ASD. They are other quantities and no local simultaneous maximum.10×- results or clinical safety claims. LS2/M1 mesial marginal0,057591mm saknar externt lokalfacit. R2The patch gate is partly trivial. (fyra tomma set); only two non-empty sets0,400/0,842% under adopted budget. Archive search includes:338 av480scans and cannot be described as whole TF2. F-lanens2305/337is another source/snapshot.\n\nFel bevarade: R1 behandlade initialt±99field file as distance, now UNKNOWN; versions/R1_before_missing_field_fix. R2 NumPy-int64 JSON-fel, versions/R2_numpy_serialization_failure. Matplotlib/NumPy-konflikt is dissolved with: PYTHONNOUSERSITE and system-Python. No thresholds changed.2 concrete fault trap checks were repaired from declared booleans to actually executed patch/witness validation before final report.\n\nNext construction: real frozen model prediction plus the same scanner/protokoll matchad oberoende lokal kanalyta eller µCT-pulpareferens. MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_PORT are exact minimum requirements. Continue on the same decision by adding this reference observations; a fourth own fixture or additional scalar TIE It's not enough.\n\nGrafdispatch: DENT-GEOM-UNCERTAINTY, lane X5-decision-seg-error. GRAPH_FEEDBACK ska bindas som PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. Missing coverage to suggest: an explicit local observation sport with fixed design/plattform, canal_wall/pulp_surface, simultaneously directed maximum error, full hazard coverage and independent physical proof; a consumer for connected_false_positive_budget. Inga native/genererade source graphs are changed.\n\nDatakatalog {DATA}; alla arrayer hashade i results.json, under3MB. Lane cirka26MB including preserved results versions. Threads1, GPU0; inget steg≥4GB. Basdatasetlicens TF2CCBY-SA4.0, STSCCBY4.0. Independent review is still missing.\n")
    put('ATTEMPTS.json', [{'round': r['id'], 'changed_operation': json.load(open(P / f'PREREG_R{i}.json'))['changed_operation'], 'outcome': r['outcome'], 'gates': r['gates'], 'parent_artifacts': json.load(open(P / f'PREREG_R{i}.json')).get('parent', json.load(open(P / 'PREREG_R1.json'))['source_parent_ids'])} for (i, r) in enumerate([r1, r2, r3], 1)])
    state('DEMO_PACKAGED_PENDING_REVIEW', results['outcome'], results['next_construction'])
